  "sourceReviewFindings": [
    "The capture checks each actual public command before supplying its archived public return; the qualifier checks exact public commands and packets across both sides and against the shared trace.",
    "The consolidator requires each raw trial to equal its own frozen functional form; its recursive comparison permits only the four declared counter paths and checks exact expected baseline/candidate values there. Within-version full signatures remain strict.",
    "The capture observes recordSource exactly once only for an actually selected Symbols return; the qualifier binds acquired events/state facts to such calls. In these four cases no Symbols return is selected.",
    "The retained qualifier reconstructs complete delta chains and checks common node metadata, common delta identities/causes/order, exact cumulative attributed revision differences and actual added node identities. This review reads that code and its retained verdict; it does not rerun that reconstruction.",
    "Independent child review confirmed the real-factory inventory adds only one Symbols owner and one family-installed program, with no removals, and preserves baseline realpath/confinement rules."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No timing or cost acceptance is established by this receipt. Official window isolation/readiness and future raw-trial comparisons remain separate gates.",
    "The four cost forms contain zero selected Symbols returns; they do not measure an active Symbols/CRAF trajectory or independently establish active acquisition semantics.",
    "Private common-node value equality and private caches are outside the retained qualification. Exact public work and the declared structural counts are the bounded claim.",
    "No new fragments occur in these captures, so the closed R2 common-fragment limitation is not exercised; no 5A fragment identifiers or exception rule was imported.",
    "The family-installed program inventory is not a catalogue of every runtime-created graph node. Actual node counts are bound by the retained capture fixture."
  ],
